MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

New fork-owned package com.noop.food (no upstream file touched):
- FoodVision: one raw-HTTP Messages API call per photo with the wearer's
  Anthropic key (AiKeyStore), image + note in one user turn, structured
  output via output_config.format json_schema; one plain retry when an
  older model rejects output_config. Never sends temperature/top_p/
  thinking/tool_choice; reads text through AiCoach.anthropicReplyText so
  the leading thinking block of Claude 5.x is skipped. Errors map to a
  FoodError enum (key, busy, offline, timeout, refusal, unreadable...).
- FoodImage: EXIF-upright downscale to 1568 px, JPEG 85 (stepping down
  only above 3.5 MB), plus a 320 px thumbnail; full photos never stored.
- FoodStore: JSON log in files/food (write-then-rename, corrupt file set
  aside), thumbnails in files/food/thumbs.
- FoodNutritionSync: mirrors each day's totals into the existing
  "nutrition-csv" lane (calories_in, protein_g, carbs_g, fat_g) so
  Explore/Compare/Data Sources show them with no reader hooks. Only days
  with photo entries are written, weight is never touched, and a cleared
  day deletes only values still equal to what the log wrote (ledger), so
  CSV imports survive.
- FoodCoachContext.line(): one compact English line for the AI Coach.

Tests: request shape and banned params, structured/fallback/refusal
parsing, retry and status mapping, day totals, lane plan, coach line,
codec round trip (27 JVM tests).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
